um holding time for achieving required finishing rolling temperatures [Data: Entities (1532, 1530, 1531, 1534); Relationships (3165, 3145, 3146, 3153)]. Billet cooling can be inefficient due to large thickness and risk of cooling corner and edge zones, and it requires specialized cooling means [Data: Entities (1538, 1537, 1554); Relationships (3131, 3130, 3183)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Finishing stand and temperature regime shape operations\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The finishing stand is where deformation is completed, reductions are increased, and rolling starts at T_H = 750–700°C; before this stand, the transfer bar can be air-cooled, and passes are rolled within the stand [Data: Entities (1289, 1308, 1330); Relationships (2868, 2828)]. Continuous operation of the finishing stand is a condition of the process [Data: Entities (1338); Relationships (2890)]. The low-temperature controlled rolling regime is needed to obtain a specified level of properties but causes production difficulties, so mill productivity and accident-free operation must be ensured [Data: Entities (1302, 1305, 1306); Relationships (2817, 2822, 2823)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Productivity and mill loads reveal trade-offs\",\n      \"explanation\": \"КПУО is associated with an increase in mill productivity and a reduction in holding time of rolled stock before the final rolling stage [Data: Entities (1519, 1521, 1551, 1549); Relationships (3180, 3138, 3137, 3178)]. However, in the КПУО variant, mill loads may not decrease, whereas they decrease in the second scheme [Data: Entities (1518); Relationships (3136)]. This trade-off is important for safe and efficient mill operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Practical implementation favors the first scheme\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The first scheme is recommended for testing and practical implementation [Data: Entities (1555); Relationships (3184)]. The schemes may be implemented on mill 3600, and controlled rolling with one holding is also a controlled rolling route [Data: Entities (1503, 1324); Relationships (3132, 2850)]. Adoption aims at minimum holding, required controlled rolling temperatures, and ensuring the specified complex of properties and flatness [Data: Entities (1534, 1562, 1481, 1514); Relationships (3153, 3193, 3118, 3119)].\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 9701, "completion_tokens": 5776, "total_tokens": 15477, "compute_duration_seconds": 24.649242162704468, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}